+# Reservations at tool readers
+
+HOLD FOR DEPLOYMENT: apply and publish only after the coordinated Rails, API,
+portal, and reader release has passed hardware acceptance.
+
+At an equipped tool, your normal successful check-in can claim your approved
+reservation from one hour before it starts through fifteen minutes after it starts.
+An earlier active reservation must finish first. Checking in at one equipped tool
+claims the entire tool/group/shop booking. If you are already using the tool, an
+eligible reservation can be associated automatically.
+
+The display alternates normal idle information with the current or next booking.
+During use it shows the earlier of your reservation end or another member's start.
+Reminders flash red; the fifteen- and five-minute reminders play a tune.
+These reminders do not change tool authorization or switch off power.
+
+Logging off voluntarily releases the rest of your whole booking. Being kicked off,
+a reader reboot, or authorization expiry does not count as voluntary release.
+A booking with no qualifying arrival can be marked **Abandoned** after fifteen
+minutes, once all participating readers have synchronized attendance. An offline
+reader can delay this decision. Abandoned bookings release availability and appear
+in history; reservation fees and invoices remain unchanged.
+
+Contact a shop manager if a reader remains unavailable or a booking needs ordinary
+administrative cancellation. Do not clear reader attendance records to force release.

