-## Slack and calendar
+## Reader attendance and released bookings
+
+**Cancelled or abandoned** includes an **Abandoned** booking immediately after no-show verification. It releases availability while retaining fees and invoices. It cannot be edited, approved or cancelled again. Voluntary owner logoff appears as **cancelled**, with its release explanation, and releases the whole booking.
+
+Only equipped reservation-enabled readers participate in automatic no-show verification. Every participating reader must synchronize its attendance, so an offline reader can delay release. If a reader remains unavailable, use ordinary cancellation for a still-active booking. Do not clear attendance records to force abandonment. See [Reservations at Tool Readers](/digital-makerspace/reservations/tool-readers).
+
+## Slack and calendar
 
 - **/reserve** works in each shop's linked Slack channel.
 - The portal keeps two read-only canvases per shop, **Today's … Reservations** and **Tomorrow's … Reservations**. A channel manager adds each one to the channel header once, with the **+** button in Slack. After that they update on their own.

